WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.120
A mountain rises across a flat valley.

2
00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:06.880
You can see the summit, but
you can't get anywhere near it.

3
00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:10.930
From where you stand, you measure
the angle of elevation of the summit.

4
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:14.030
Then you walk a measured
distance straight towards it,

5
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.480
and measure again.

6
00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:17.280
The angle is steeper now.

7
00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:19.890
Two angles and one walked distance.

8
00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:22.480
How could that possibly
give you the height?

9
00:00:22.530 --> 00:00:25.590
In this mission, you'll
use angles of elevation.

10
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.500
Each one is measured
up from the horizontal.

11
00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:33.040
You'll meet the sine rule, which works
even when a triangle has no right angle.

12
00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:37.300
And you'll learn to split one
hard problem into two triangles.

13
00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:41.800
Your mission: explain how you can find
a mountain's height without climbing it.
